module examples.err_layout_implicit_padding

# plans/M7.md decision 4: "No implicit padding." An ordinary compiler
# silently inserts three bytes here so `sector` lands 4-byte aligned; this
# one refuses and says how many bytes it would have had to invent. The fix
# is to say what you meant — `@offset(0x004)` for a hole, or reorder the
# fields so none is needed.

@layout(dma, endian=little)
struct Request:
    kind: u8
    sector: u32
